cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MedChange-VLM in your research, please cite this software."
title: "MedChange-VLM: Safety-Aware Multimodal AI for Longitudinal Chest X-Ray Change Analysis"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-08-18

authors:
  - family-names: "Munde"
    given-names: "Aniket"

abstract: >
  MedChange-VLM is a research prototype for longitudinal chest X-ray
  change analysis. It combines BiomedCLIP-based temporal classification
  with Qwen2.5-VL multimodal reasoning, evidence fusion, uncertainty
  estimation, selective-risk policies, human-review routing,
  evidence-grounded reporting, FastAPI inference, and a Streamlit
  research interface.

keywords:
  - medical artificial intelligence
  - chest x-ray
  - longitudinal imaging
  - vision-language model
  - multimodal AI
  - BiomedCLIP
  - Qwen2.5-VL
  - selective prediction
  - uncertainty estimation
  - biomedical imaging
  - QLoRA

repository-code: "https://github.com/AniketMunde/MedChange-VLM"

license: MIT